codex
**Findings**
- Medium: [src/lib/server/ops/get-degraded-impact-diagnostics.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/ops/get-degraded-impact-diagnostics.js#L134) ignored `disruptionEmphasis.affectedModeKeys` unless trust/source had already degraded, so strained modes could disappear from ops diagnostics. Fixed by merging disruption-emphasis evidence into affected areas and covering it in [tests/unit/ops-health.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/ops-health.test.mjs#L390).
- Medium: [src/lib/server/ops/get-degraded-impact-diagnostics.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/ops/get-degraded-impact-diagnostics.js#L274) still reported “healthy” areas during `snapshotState: "fallback"`, which overstated operator confidence on unconfirmed reads. Fixed by suppressing healthy-area claims for fallback/overall-impact cases and adding regression coverage in [tests/unit/ops-health.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/ops-health.test.mjs#L427).
- Medium: [src/features/ops/ops-shell-view.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/ops/ops-shell-view.js#L35) only defaulted when `diagnostics` was fully absent; partial payloads could surface blank labels/details in the UI. Fixed by normalizing partial diagnostics payloads and covering that path in [tests/unit/ops-shell.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/ops-shell.test.mjs#L155).

Review outcome is `Approve`. I updated the story record in [docs/sprint-artifacts/3-3-diagnose-degraded-impact-by-signal-and-scope.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/3-3-diagnose-degraded-impact-by-signal-and-scope.md#L3) with the review notes and set sprint tracking to `done` in [docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml#L25).

Verification: `npm run validate` passed. I left the unrelated log change untouched.
